A Powerhouse package's **runtime** shape is `DocumentModelLib` (`packages/shared/document-model/types.ts:1703`), not a `VetraPackage` with a `modules` wrapper:

```typescript
type DocumentModelLib = {
  manifest: Manifest;
  documentModels: readonly DocumentModelModule[];
  editors: readonly EditorModule[];
  subgraphs?: readonly SubgraphModule[];
  upgradeManifests?: readonly UpgradeManifest<readonly number[]>[];
  processorFactory?: ProcessorFactoryBuilder;
};
```

Two things to note: `processorFactory` is a **single builder, not an array**, and `upgradeManifests` is a first-class member.

The **manifest** shape is `ManifestSchema` (`packages/shared/document-model/schemas.ts:908`): `name`, optional `description` / `category` / `image` / `publisher`, then `documentModels`, `apps`, `editors`, `processors`, `subgraphs`, plus optional `config` and `pwa`. Note `apps` — drive apps are a first-class manifest section.

Connect reads packages via `useVetraPackages()`, which returns `DocumentModelLib[]`. The setter is `setVetraPackageManager(packageManager)` (`packages/reactor-browser/src/hooks/vetra-packages.ts:31`).

**Names that do not exist in code.** `subgraphModules`, `importScriptModules` and `processorModules` all return zero hits, as does `setVetraPackages()` — the latter survives only in `apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/05-EditorsUI/01-ReactHooks.md`, which documents an API the code does not have.

The registry ambition around packages — publish, discover, fork, extend, monetize, with authors sharing in value generated downstream — is unchanged.

_Source-verified 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse source at v6.2.2-dev.45._
